        <definition>SDK_CAPI CUVIS_STATUS SDK_CCALL cuvis_measurement_load</definition>
        <argsstring>(const CUVIS_CHAR *i_path, CUVIS_MESU *o_pMesu)</argsstring>
        <name>cuvis_measurement_load</name>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="cuvis_8h_1ad6fd13ac609b8cbfad5f49e5ff0e11d3" kindref="member">CUVIS_CHAR</ref> *</type>
          <declname>i_path</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="cuvis_8h_1a79fa4e0f6faf8ddaabf6ee66dfa00d3e" kindref="member">CUVIS_MESU</ref> *</type>
          <declname>o_pMesu</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Load a measurement from disk. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The measurement is a cu3 file - and if fragmented some additional tiff files with a postfix, e.g. _cube.tiff To load the file, all fragmented parts must be in the same directory. Fragmented files must not be renamed.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">i_path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the file path of the measurement </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">o_pMesu</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the handle of the measurement. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><ref refid="group__cuvis__returns_1ggaa06c62ba25240f4763da0e590ebf3b9dad52787b0cfb0da2c053a68bcdc54bc6f" kindref="member">status_ok</ref>, if the measurement could be loaded. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
