        <definition>SDK_CAPI CUVIS_STATUS SDK_CCALL cuvis_measurement_deep_copy</definition>
        <argsstring>(CUVIS_MESU i_mesu, CUVIS_MESU *o_pMesu)</argsstring>
        <name>cuvis_measurement_deep_copy</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="cuvis_8h_1a79fa4e0f6faf8ddaabf6ee66dfa00d3e" kindref="member">CUVIS_MESU</ref></type>
          <declname>i_mesu</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="cuvis_8h_1a79fa4e0f6faf8ddaabf6ee66dfa00d3e" kindref="member">CUVIS_MESU</ref> *</type>
          <declname>o_pMesu</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>create a deep copy of a measurement</para>
<para>All operations on a measurement are performed on the same object. If different processing needs to be perfomed on a measurement It should be deep-copied. The copied meausrement&apos;s name will be changed to end with &quot;_copy&quot;</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">i_mesu</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The measurement copy source. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">o_pMesu</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The copy will be linked to the handle given. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
